        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189964965?u=5e030a50f854f5d4d5c0c9e3e0d2599fe830e4f2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Fixes internal links pointing to nonexistent pages, found by checking every <code class=\"notranslate\">/en-US/docs/</code> link against both the file tree and <code class=\"notranslate\">_redirects.txt</code>:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>WebAssembly</strong>: <code class=\"notranslate\">Tag</code> docs linked <code class=\"notranslate\">exnref</code> via <code class=\"notranslate\">Reference/Types/exnref</code>; the page lives at <code class=\"notranslate\">Reference/Value_types/exnref</code> (matching the links already used in the exception handling and tag definition docs).</li>\n<li><strong>XSLT</strong>: <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;xsl:stylesheet&gt;</code> docs linked <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;xsl:for-each-group&gt;</code>, an XSLT 2.0 element MDN does not document; converted to plain code text.</li>\n<li><strong>SVGElement</strong>: the events list included <code class=\"notranslate\">abort</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">resize</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">scroll</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">unload</code>, whose pages do not exist (these events were dropped from SVG2); removed those entries, keeping <code class=\"notranslate\">error</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">load</code> which have pages.</li>\n<li><strong>WebXR</strong>: four pages linked the deleted \"Using gamepads in WebXR applications\" article; retargeted to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebXR_Device_API/Inputs#advanced_controllers_using_the_gamepad_object\" rel=\"nofollow\">Advanced controllers using the gamepad object</a> section of the Inputs guide, where this content now lives.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not touched: links to plausibly-planned pages (<code class=\"notranslate\">MediaTrackConstraints.resizeMode</code>, MathML global attributes, CycleTracker tutorial parts, <code class=\"notranslate\">import/source</code>) and the ~60 broken links in the WebDriver reference, which look like they need a maintainer decision (happy to file a separate issue about those).</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44830",
            "title": "Fix broken internal links (WebXR, SVGElement, WebAssembly, XSLT)",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T05:27:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-20T05:26:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rajanpanth",
                "url": "https://github.com/rajanpanth"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189964965?u=5e030a50f854f5d4d5c0c9e3e0d2599fe830e4f2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Per the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/MDN/Writing_guidelines/Writing_style_guide#spelling\" rel=\"nofollow\">writing style guide</a>, MDN uses American English spelling.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\"labelled\" → \"labeled\" in 8 pages (prose and image alt text in Learn web development and the Certificate Transparency guide)</li>\n<li>\"artefact\" → \"artifact\" in the <code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.NumberFormat.prototype.format()</code> docs</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Deliberately excluded: verbatim Firefox error messages (\"functions cannot be labelled\"), <code class=\"notranslate\">aria-labelledby</code> contexts, the <code class=\"notranslate\">favourite-colour</code> example extension, and the style guide's own incorrect-spelling examples.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spelling-only change; no content changes.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44829",
            "title": "Use American English: \"labelled\" → \"labeled\", \"artefact\" → \"artifact\"",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T05:17:43.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-20T05:17:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rajanpanth",
                "url": "https://github.com/rajanpanth"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189964965?u=5e030a50f854f5d4d5c0c9e3e0d2599fe830e4f2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Fixes indefinite article usage before vowel-sound initialisms: \"a HTML\" → \"an HTML\" in 12 pages and \"a XML\" → \"an XML\" in the XSLT common errors guide.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Affected pages include glossary entries (boolean/HTML, markup, XHTML), <code class=\"notranslate\">Element.innerHTML</code>, the <code class=\"notranslate\">FormData</code> constructor, <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLIFrameElement.srcdoc</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLMetaElement</code>, the PAC file guide, CSP <code class=\"notranslate\">script-src</code>, both MathML guides, and the Rust-to-Wasm tutorial.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Grammar-only change; no content changes.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44828",
            "title": "Fix grammar: \"a HTML\" → \"an HTML\" (13 pages)",
