            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF153 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">farthest-corner</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">closest-corner</code> radius values for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/basic-shape/ellipse\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">ellipse()</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/basic-shape/circle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">circle()</code></a> in Nightly in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2037673\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2037673</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the docs to include the feature. It adds the two new keywords, and an example that allows you to see the effect of selecting the keywords and also moving the center of the circle within its reference box.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4666421187\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44459\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44459/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44459\">#44459</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44827",
            "title": "FF153 CSS basic shape closest-/farthest-corner",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-20T05:13:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-20T05:08:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189964965?u=5e030a50f854f5d4d5c0c9e3e0d2599fe830e4f2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Fixes the misspelling \"withing\" → \"within\" in three pages:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">Performance.measure()</code> (track-entry grouping description)</li>\n<li>CSS replaced element properties guide (<code class=\"notranslate\">object-fit</code> description)</li>\n<li>SVG attribute reference (event handler attributes note)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spelling-only change; no content changes.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44826",
